From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Almeida Barrios <gabarrios2006@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:04:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] engine: adding someone to a call that is already a group call
 sends the invite to the call, naming only the invited user

inviteParticipant and ringParticipant always sent the offer of the first invite: to the invited person, with a <destination> and the whole roster in <group_info>. That is what turns a one-to-one call into a group call. Once the server holds the group call it answers nothing to that offer, so nobody rang while the caller was told the person had been invited (user logs, 2026-11-16: the first person added joined, the next six invites got no ack and no group update).

WhatsApp Web 2.3000.1052669929, captured on 2026-11-17 adding a person to a group call of two connected participants, sends <call to="<call-id>@call"><offer call-id call-creator><audio enc="opus" rate="16000"/><net medium="2"/><invite><user jid user_pn><device jid/>...</user></invite></offer></call>, and the server acks it with the roster, the user in state "outgoing".

A call is taken for a group call the server holds once a group update arrived for it (the ack of the first invite is one). The phone number comes from the roster when ringing someone on the list, else from the LID store; without one the user goes without user_pn.

Validated: engine_group_invite_test.go (five tests), go test . ./signaling green. Not yet validated on a live call.
